pr_comments:
@sc68cal The intent is to fail fast when non-blocking IO is in use (see the original PR https://github.com/ansible/ansible/pull/77639 and issue https://github.com/ansible/ansible/issues/77660).

As for the issue reported in https://github.com/ansible/ansible/issues/79633, I don't think we should be adding platform specific logic and error messages for unsupported controller platforms. Any checks we add for unsupported platforms would go untested. If we added this check, there would likely be other places in the code that would also result in a traceback on unsupported platforms. Changing them would result in yet more untested code.

There seems to be little value in trying to gracefully handle this specific case, and none for users running Ansible on a supported platform.

